## Summary Checklist

When starting a new Godot project, implement these patterns:

**Core Systems:**
- [ ] Create `MessageBus` autoload for event communication
- [ ] Create `BaseManager` class for manager inheritance
- [ ] Create `SaveManager` for persistence
- [ ] Create `SettingsManager` for configuration
- [ ] Create `SceneManager` for transitions
- [ ] Create `AppConstants` for centralized constants

**Data Management:**
- [ ] Define data schemas (JSON structure or Resource classes)
- [ ] Create Resource catalogs for asset collections
- [ ] Implement data validation on load

**UI System:**
- [ ] Create base UI component scripts with signals
- [ ] Implement standard animations (open/close/fade)
- [ ] Build pause menu with settings panel
- [ ] Implement notification/toast system

**Architecture:**
- [ ] Use deferred initialization for all autoloads
- [ ] Validate system dependencies on startup
- [ ] Emit events through MessageBus, never call directly
- [ ] Keep UI, logic, and data separate

